          "#### Repositories",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = \"<a href='https://osf.io/msfcn' target='_blank'>osf.io/msfcn<\/a>\", \n    Platform = \"osf\", \"All Files\" = 3L, \"Data Files\" = 2L, \"Code Files\" = 0L, \n    READMEs = 0L, Archives = 0L), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = c(\"tbl_df\", \n\"tbl\", \"data.frame\"))\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Files",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Repository = c(\"https://osf.io/msfcn\", \"https://osf.io/msfcn\", \n\"https://osf.io/msfcn\"), File = c(\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/5qsc6/' target='_blank'>Data_Experiment_1.xlsx<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/4v5hd/' target='_blank'>Data_Experiment_2.xlsx<\/a>\", \n\"<a href='https://osf.io/download/x6n74/' target='_blank'>Suplemental Material_Chairs used for data collection.docx<\/a>\"\n), Size = c(\"251 kB\", \"181.7 kB\", \"122.4 kB\"), Type = c(\"data\", \n\"data\", \"text\")), row.names = c(NA, -3L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### README Files\n\nREADME files are a way to document the contents and structure of a folder, helping users locate the information they need. You can use a README to document changes to a repository, and explain how files are named. Please consider adding a README to each repository or including 'README' in the name of your overview document.",
